--[[
    Dummies vs Noobs Premium - v2.7 (bug-fixed)
    qcrylic

    Kept from v2.4: teardown, double-buffered NPC cache, shared lib, HUD settings,
    status indicator, throttled notifications, prompt cache.

    Fixed in v2.5:
      1.  config.hud is merged with defaults - an old saved config missing
          fadeDuration/showStatusIndicator no longer errors or disables the HUD
      2.  HUDCoreGui / CoreGui / PlayerGui parent fallback (gethui first)
      3.  workspace.CurrentCamera read per use instead of captured once
      4.  mouse ray filters the local character (was filtering the camera)
      5.  humanoid Died:Once is registered once per humanoid (was re-added on
          every scan, leaking up to 300*N connections per 10 minutes)
      6.  melee / Mercy Kill tools in the Backpack are equipped before firing
          (firing a Backpack tool is a no-op on the server)
      7.  namecall hook: executor function checks, rollback on failure, jitter
          applied to the real Vector3 argument (args[3] does not exist for
          melee - VerifyHit is called with (humanoid, token))
      8.  all long-running loops respect a generation counter; a re-exec stops
          them without coroutine.close on a thread suspended in task.wait
      9.  NPC scans, attack batches, HUD updates and heartbeat work are pcall'd
          so one bad frame cannot kill the loop
      10. prompt cache connection stored and disconnected on re-exec; prompts
          are also matched against ActionText
      11. HUD: finite GetTextSize bounds, guarded task.cancel, top-left anchor
          fixed, "hits" wording
      12. toggle cross-reset uses pcall + SetValue/Set fallback
      13. killauraEnabled is no longer restored from a stale config (the toggle
          is the source of truth), so a saved `true` cannot look armed while off

    v2.6 (second pass):
      14. killaura loops use a run id instead of coroutine.close; a rapid
          off/on can no longer leave two attack loops running, and no thread is
          closed while parked in task.wait
      15. the __namecall hook is published to getgenv and unwound on the next
          execution; hooks no longer stack one per re-exec, and _G.multiplier
          is cleared by teardown
      16. backpack auto-equip is throttled to 2/s instead of once per attack
          tick, and Mercy Kill only fires once the tool is actually in the
          Character
      17. the attack loop calls scanNPCs(false), so a child add or a humanoid
          death is picked up immediately instead of up to 2s later

    v2.7 (review pass):
      18. attackBatch equips before the isHoldingTool() gate; with empty hands
          the backpack auto-equip was unreachable, so killaura stayed dead after
          every respawn
      19. an APU without a Pilot child no longer throws inside scanNPCs and
          aborts the entire NPC scan
      20. restored config flags are reflected in the toggle defaults, and the
          two Mercy modes are de-conflicted on load
      21. Auto Vote waits voteCooldown (10s) between invokes instead of calling
          the Vote remote about once a second for the whole session
      22. landmine cleared notifications use the throttle helper
      23. third-party libraries are downloaded through a guarded loader that
          names the failing source instead of erroring on a nil chunk
      24. HUD: text aligns per anchor, and a stale fade callback can no longer
          hide a re-created background
      25. mobile button no longer points at an empty asset id; Spawn Noob Units
          labels itself client-side only; Infinite PDC/Ammo note added
]]

